- Keep canonical prose concise English. Format user-facing reports with `communication` while preserving machine tokens.
- Keep runtime-facing Markdown within the declared 50-line target and 100-line hard maximum.
- Write a short Change Report when reporting is installed.
{{PROFILE_OPERATING_RULES}}

## Profile review

- Review profile scope only during harness construction or when a requested capability falls outside the installed profile.
- Recommend `adaptive` when work becomes recurring, long-running, memory-dependent, or requires measured harness improvement.
- Recommend `governed` when work requires audit controls, developer-understanding evidence, or a Learning Gate.
- Recommend a lower scope when optional capabilities remain unused or maintenance cost exceeds their value.
- Only the user may confirm a profile change. Never add or remove profile-owned files automatically.
- A downgrade requires an exact preservation and removal plan before user confirmation.

